    "logic": "Route nested vector bands through editable letterforms. The RKC reference default uses a wide R above K and C, constructed rectilinear source-style glyphs, miter joins and inward channels. Other titles, including other three-letter words, use complete word lines by default; the bespoke blocks and arrangement apply only to RKC. Single-line and individual-letter grids are explicit alternatives, and glyphs can keep their font proportions instead of filling each cell. Font outlines fill nonzero, so overlapping variable-font contours never become false counters. All letters share one distance field: outward expansion merges neighbouring channels instead of overprinting them, and the layout gives way so outer channels stay on the paper. Protected counters keep their size and their own rings while the exterior expands.",
